}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(B) & =min\\{9,\\,3,\\,0,\\,7\\}=0 \\\\ max(B) & =max\\{9,\\,3,\\,0,\\,7\\}=9\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573773 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1069 "q-181992" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1071 "What are the minimum and maximum of the set $C=\\{-7,\\,-1,\\,-4,\\,-5\\}?$\n\n$min(C)=$\n{{field-1}}\n\n$\\,max(C)=$\n{{field-2}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26063449-9909-57c8-a81e-1b4914486c12" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573880 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that \n\n- ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{max}\\in S$ and $x\\le {x}_{max}$ for all $x\\in S,$ and\n\n- ${x}_{min}$ is the minimum of a set $S$ if ${x}_{min}\\in S$ and ${x}_{min}\\le x$ for all $x\\in S.$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}min(C) & =min\\{-7,\\,-1,\\,-4,\\,-5\\}=-7 \\\\ max(C) & =max\\{-7,\\,-1,\\,-4,\\,-5\\}=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186573789 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1069 "q-182005" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1071 "Complete the following reasoning about the set $S=(-\\infty ,-2):$\n\nThe value $-2$ is not the maximum of the set $S$ because {{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2b1de8af-4757-54e2-a638-9811d61ed9c2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186573881 #edb/ref 1074 "Recall that ${x}_{max}$ is the maximum of a set $S$ if